# ── Data ── all of this is regenerable, and far too large for git.
#
# data/raw      (382 MB) DWR geodatabases. steps/01 re-downloads them.
# data/cache    (249 MB) Planet API responses. NOT in git, but do NOT delete —
#               this is ~115,000 processing units of paid work. Back it up
#               separately; losing it means paying for it again.
# data/processed(201 MB) derived tables, rebuilt from cache for free.
data/raw/
data/cache/
data/interim/
data/processed/

# ── Build output ──
# The published site lives in docs/ and IS committed — GitHub Pages serves it.
# The standalone bundle is not: it is ~9 MB and changes on every rebuild, so
# committing it would bloat the repo history fast. Attach it to a GitHub
# Release when you want people to download it.
docs/farms-on-the-move.html

